# File: tests/bdd/features/scaffold-plugin-repo-session-start-hooks.feature
# Generated from: specs/215-judge-launcher-detach-in-the-scaffold-scenarios-by-process-state-not-a-2-second-wall-clock/requirements.md
Feature: Launcher detach is judged by process state, not wall-clock time

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: A launcher passes when it exits 0 while its child is still running
    Given a fake Blender and a fake UE editor that record their PID and argv and keep running until stopped
    When scripts/start-blender-mcp.sh and scripts/start-unreal-mcp.sh each run against their fake
    Then each script exits 0 while the fake child it started is still alive
    And the fake UE editor's recorded argv holds -ModelContextProtocolStartServer and -ModelContextProtocolPort=18088
    And both fake children are stopped afterwards

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: A launcher that waits for its child fails the detach check
    Given a synthetic launcher that starts the fake child and waits for it
    When it runs with a child that exits after 1 second, and again with a child that keeps running under a 3 second bound
    Then the detach check fails the first run because the child is gone
    And the detach check fails the second run because the launcher did not return

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: A slow launcher that detaches still passes
    Given a synthetic launcher that sleeps 2.5 seconds before detaching the fake child
    When it runs
    Then it takes more than 2 seconds
    And the detach check passes because it exited 0 while its child was still running
